    "score": 421,
    "text": "My company is pretty paranoid about leaking IP to the frontier labs through prompts, so we&#x27;ve all been diligent about disabling data sharing in Codex&#x2F;Claude Code&#x2F;etc. But yesterday my coworkers and I noticed that the setting had been silently reenabled in Codex. None of us knowingly opted back in.<p>You can check your settings here: https:&#x2F;&#x2F;chatgpt.com&#x2F;settings&#x2F;data-controls. Look for &quot;Improve the model for everyone&quot;.<p>Curious if this is an isolated issue or something more widespread.<p>EDIT: looks like this has been noted before https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49643556<p>EDIT: apparently you can also turn off data sharing here: https:&#x2F;&#x2F;privacy.openai.com&#x2F;policies?modal=take-control",
